action "Read candidate.py and baseline_reference.py, diagnose an observed limitation, check primary nearest work, and implement a feasible candidate. Write proposal.json containing study (matching study_schema), parent_trial (existing trial ID), and variants (1-4 objects with distinct name, file basename ending .py, role candidate/control, config object, and note). At least one candidate is required. Add key ablations or matched controls for the claimed mechanism when feasible; reference existing matched trials as controls where justified. Each variant is a standalone module. Do not run training. New architecture choices come from evidence; industry cards do not mandate them."
candidate_api {"Model": "Model(feature_map, model_id=..., gpu=0, **kwargs) -> torch.nn.Module; optional MultiTaskModel utilities. forward(inputs) returns {label+\"_pred\": probability [B,1]} for all four tasks. Host places the module on the assigned GPU.", "architecture_scope": "Whole-model design for unified modeling. Model need not inherit the initial reference, retain its pooling, or use separate task towers; representations, interactions, routing and readout can all be replaced.", "lineage": "parent_trial records the empirical comparison and evidence lineage. A complete rewrite may have no inherited architectural components.", "proposal_unit": "Coordinated structural changes implementing one coherent mechanism are allowed; isolate their effects through planned replacement, component or factorial controls.", "meta": "Read-only UniRank FeatureMap: features (ordered specs, sources, vocab_size), labels, data_dir. Full framework reference files are available through tools.py.", "batch": ["inputs=(batch_dict,item_dict,history_mask,multi_task_history_masks)", "batch_dict: categorical user/context features int64[B]; current labels and lookup metadata are removed by host", "item_dict: item_id,cate_id,campaign_id,customer_id,brand,price_bucket,action, each int64[B,101]; last position is current target, preceding100 are pre-padded history", "history_mask: float 0/1 [B,100]; four task masks: [B,100]; use only masked history", "Target action is always zero (unknown/padding), never a current label. Historical feedback policy is frozen in protocol.history_policy.", "Historical item_id is a previous advertisement ID. Shopping events used to create auxiliary labels are only matched by user/category/brand.", "No raw timestamps, event-time deltas, raw user IDs, full future histories, current labels or global sample indexes are supplied to forward."], "task_labels": ["is_click", "cart", "fav", "buy"], "primary": "Validation is_click ROC-AUC. All four AUC/Logloss values and mean AUC are reported; auxiliary mean is not the selection score.", "optional": ["Literal CONFIG dict for model architecture only; all frozen host parameters are rejected.", "Model.training_loss(inputs, probabilities[B,4], train_labels[B,4]) -> finite differentiable scalar; labels supplied only during training. Default is sum of four unweighted BCEs."], "ownership": "Edit candidate modules/proposal only. No filesystem/network operations in model source. Imports: torch,numpy,math,typing,copy,functools,collections,itertools,dataclasses,contextlib,unirank,model_zoo. Host owns training, input filtering and scoring.", "local_checks": "Coding jail has no torch; check syntax/source there. Host trains and scores. Do not install or train inside coding jail.", "training": "From scratch; same frozen data, seed, epochs, batch, history limit and dense AdamW / embedding Adagrad. Architecture may be rewritten completely. Retain causal controls and account for added parameters/computation."}
